    <innernamespace refid="namespaceasyncdb">asyncdb</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Implementation for asyncresultmapper: Converts one row into a JSON object using name- and value-based type inference. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This file implements the row-to-JSON conversion. For each column it checks whether the value is SQL NULL, whether the column is a known boolean or identifier field, whether the text looks like JSON, and otherwise keeps the text as a string. The first-row and all-row helpers simply call the row mapper in a loop or at index zero.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: Async controller methods receive a Drogon Result and must return JSON to the HTTP layer. This file performs that translation and deliberately mirrors the older synchronous <ref refid="classDatabase_1a31f82e76631ee18c6314141ecb35e89e" kindref="member">Database::executeQuery</ref> outcomes: nulls stay null, the active flag is a boolean, ids are numbers, and json/jsonb columns become nested JSON. Because parsing errors are caught and the raw text is kept, one unusual database value cannot crash a whole list response. Without this file, the async database path could not produce the same JSON contract that the rest of the API relies on.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Drogon result sets, rows and fields: <ulink url="https://drogon.docsforge.com/master/database/">https://drogon.docsforge.com/master/database/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>jsoncons JSON values and parsing: <ulink url="https://danielaparker.github.io/jsoncons/">https://danielaparker.github.io/jsoncons/</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::string_view (a cheap, non-owning look at text): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++ exceptions and catch-all handlers: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>C++20 coroutines: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/coroutines</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
